---
title: App Sign-Out State Machine
---

%% Deprecated by Identity Authority inversion.
%% logout is acme/www session mutation; /sign/out is redirect-only if retained.

%% Current runtime vocabulary. Future canonical lifecycle terminology is defined in
%% docs/security/idp-flow-lifecycle.md and is not implemented yet.
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> REQUESTED: authenticated sign-out submitted

  REQUESTED --> ACCESS_DISCARDED: access cookie discarded
  REQUESTED --> FAILED: access discard failed

  ACCESS_DISCARDED --> TOKEN_REVOKED: token revoke primitive completed
  ACCESS_DISCARDED --> FAILED: token revoke failed

  TOKEN_REVOKED --> AWAITING_EXPIRY: wait for token expiry boundary
  TOKEN_REVOKED --> FAILED: expiry boundary failed

  AWAITING_EXPIRY --> COMPLETED: cookies cleared and session reset
  AWAITING_EXPIRY --> FAILED: reset failed

  note right of ACCESS_DISCARDED
    ACCESS_DISCARDED is the POST-operation refusal
    boundary. After this state, the browser must not
    be able to perform authenticated writes.
  end note

  note right of COMPLETED
    Already-signed-out replay is an idempotent result,
    not a persisted sign-out cycle state.
  end note

  COMPLETED --> [*]
  FAILED --> [*]
